{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1077512-what-is-modus-operandi-of-nwo-against-vampires","id":1077512,"title":"What is modus operandi of NWO against vampires?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-04-12T21:40:02-07:00","id":1077512,"title":"What is modus operandi of NWO against vampires?","content":"Do they intervene in force if Sabbat leeches rampaging across a city, feeding upon and brutalizing and torturing so-called 'cattle'? Or they just watch and do nothing, let things go hang?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11780-posthumanity","name":"Posthumanity","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T21:42:21-07:00","id":1077513,"title":"","content":"Watch and observe, if possible &quot;leak&quot; information to the cam or forward to other conventions (read int-x) to handle if it's a pressing matter. Vampires are a little low on the priority list of reality deviants.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T22:25:35-07:00","id":1077532,"title":"","content":"If the New World Order does anything, it'll be indirectly. Most important is the preservation of the Consensus, which will involve covering up or discrediting more overtly supernatural stories of reality deviance. Think about it like Men In Black. Witnesses will get a visit from guys in mirror shades, who wave neuralizers around and tell people what they &quot;really&quot; saw. Strings in the local media will be pulled to kill stories that reveal too much, and plants inside the police will see to it that damning evidence is lost or replaced. If some law enforcement aid needs to get disciplinary action for losing that evidence, it's a small price to pay. If they can, the NWO will plant false evidence to lead police towards a more mundane criminal or explanation for events.<br /> <br /> All of this assumes, of course, that the local Kindred aren't doing their part to maintain their little Masquerade. Of course, the NWO may be trying to cover things up, only for their machinations to run headlong into some Camarilla elder's similar machinations of the same nature. This may result in the two working at cross purposes, or making changes so large they attract attention to the cover ups.<br /> <br /> If the Sabbat are using ghouls, and the NWO realizes this, they may pull strings to have those ghouls arrested by police or the FBI. Or else pull strings in local government to get some of their resources compromised. Havens demolished, revenue sources stopped, etc. The Syndicate might be tapped for this sort of work as well, being the financial experts they are.<br /> <br /> The NWO is only going to act violently if they don't think they have an alternative. In that case, they're definitely going to call in backup from Iteration X, and the Progenitors of Damage Control too, if Tzimisce flesh-crafters become a problem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T23:21:11-07:00","id":1077540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BurritoMage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1077512-what-is-modus-operandi-of-nwo-against-vampires?p=1077513#post1077513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Watch and observe, if possible &quot;leak&quot; information to the cam or forward to other conventions (read int-x) to handle if it's a pressing matter. Vampires are a little low on the priority list of reality deviants.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have always wondered why on earth leeches are so low on the priority list. Aren't vampires the most active and dire threat of consensus?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","name":"Numinous","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T23:57:09-07:00","id":1077545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Numinous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1077512-what-is-modus-operandi-of-nwo-against-vampires?p=1077540#post1077540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have always wondered why on earth leeches are so low on the priority list. Aren't vampires the most active and dire threat of consensus?</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, it's easier for them to rock the Consensus, on account of them being mysteriously immune to Paradox and Disbelief (and, unlike the changing breeds, have no built-in mechanism for covering their tracks). But it's for that same reason - and their predatory unlifestyle - that Vampires also have the greatest incentive to <i>police themselves</i> when it comes to keeping the secret from mortals. They do the Technocracy's job for them, for both themselves and for other supernatural weirdness. The Kindred are kind enough to see to their own secrecy, leaving the Union free to handle less accommodating reality deviants.<br /> <br /> What's more, they're damn good at it. Memory alteration is one of the most common powers available to Vampires, and they can enslave people with their addictive blood if that doesn't take. Point being, while they can be an enormous threat to the Consensus, they have just as much a vested interest in keeping it as the Technocracy does, and are capable of doing so.<br /> <br /> They're SO capable of hiding, in fact, that even the Technocracy is woefully ignorant of just how extensive the hemophage problem really is. The Union assumes vampires are rare. If they knew the full scope of the Kindred population, they'd probably take them far more seriously.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":6156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","user":"Bluecho","date":". 04-13-2017, 02:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T00:09:47-07:00","id":1077549,"title":"","content":"Vampires aren't trying to win the hearts and minds of the sleepers that define the consensus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T00:26:41-07:00","id":1077552,"title":"","content":"So the Camarilla are successful in containing and regulating Sabbat, FoS, Giovanni, Baali and other recalcitrant factions and curbing their wanton excesses? If so, how could Cam manage to sustain losses and casualties accrued from continued open hostilities?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11780,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11780-posthumanity","user":"Posthumanity","date":". 04-13-2017, 03:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11780-posthumanity","name":"Posthumanity","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T00:35:23-07:00","id":1077554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Posthumanity</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1077512-what-is-modus-operandi-of-nwo-against-vampires?p=1077552#post1077552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the Camarilla are successful in containing and regulating Sabbat, FoS, Giovanni, Baali and other recalcitrant factions and curbing their wanton excesses?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, those other groups are also trying to hide their actions. If they didn't, they'd be found and destroyed quickly. Granted, some groups try harder than others, but even the Sabbat is capable of maintaining the Masquerade (grudgingly). Usually by making enough witnesses disappear that no one knows for sure what happened.<br /> <br /> &quot;Regulation&quot; is a loaded word, and not necessary in this context. The other groups don't need to stop committing atrocities. They just need to keep them secret, or disguise them so people take them as regular, banal atrocities. This is both to hide from mortals, and from other Kindred who take the Masquerade (and whatever other ethical standards) more seriously. Or just hate infernalists, in the case of the Baali. Everybody is extra careful to stay secret, because there are conspiracies within conspiracies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T00:36:43-07:00","id":1077555,"title":"","content":"Because the Cam isn't an open warfare kinda sect. They don't launch regional Crusades, hold bloody trial by combats because reasons or draw attention from third parties that would endanger their existence.<br /> <br /> They also aren't the &quot;police&quot; of the kindred, they don't regulate the independent clans since they have a stake (no pun intended) in the masquerade as well and I think your view on the sabbat running rampant in their domains is a little misinformed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13009,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","user":"BurritoMage","date":". 04-13-2017, 03:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T01:01:49-07:00","id":1077563,"title":"","content":"So Cam-Sabbat battle casualty rates are generally lower than Tradition-Technocracy or Werewolves-Wyrm rates?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11780-posthumanity","name":"Posthumanity","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T01:12:25-07:00","id":1077568,"title":"","content":"Depends on the chronicle you want to run, statistics aren't really a thing in white wolf remember. Cities falling to the sabbat is more of a meta plot thing then the norm. <br /> <br /> A prince might occasionally have a pack come through and cause a breach that the city would have to spend resources and influence to clean up then a annual full on crusade.<br /> <br /> If you want an idea on how to run a sabbat city in the first world read Montreal by night.<br /> <br /> Edit: Back on topic, if they do decide to intervene it blows what ever cover they had to any tradition mages who pay attention to the going on's of other supernaturals in the area.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13009,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","user":"BurritoMage","date":". 04-13-2017, 05:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T02:11:46-07:00","id":1077581,"title":"","content":"So Masquerade is being maintained even Sabbat-held city such as Montreal or Mexico City?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11780-posthumanity","name":"Posthumanity","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T02:24:17-07:00","id":1077583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Posthumanity</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1077512-what-is-modus-operandi-of-nwo-against-vampires?p=1077581#post1077581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So Masquerade is being maintained even Sabbat-held city such as Montreal or Mexico City?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, elders still remember the burning times. Packs that can't keep it in their pants and think it's 30 days of night every night get sent to rough house in cam cities by the archbishop or become very acquainted with the Templar because they threaten sect security.<br /> <br /> Now the methods of how that masquerade are enforced will vary, a lone witness might find themselves on a packs menu rather then getting a mind wipe. If it's a shit part of town it's just another crime statistic after all. If I recall correctly in Montreal there are established hunting areas where if a tourist were to go missing it's no big deal.<br /> <br /> They still let their hair down from time to time for certain seasonal rites, but those are rarely held in view of the mortal masses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13009,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","user":"BurritoMage","date":". 04-13-2017, 05:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T02:45:14-07:00","id":1077593,"title":"","content":"Moreover, the Masquerade has been running for so long, it's built up a bit of a &quot;buffer&quot;. Primarily this buffer is the gulf between regular people (who want to believe that vampires are just a myth), and <i>vampire hunters</i>. Those who hunt monsters are likely to be attracted to obvious vampire activity before anyone else is even willing to entertain the notion. Most of the public and the powers that be think that vampire hunters are crazy, and don't listen to their stories of undead monsters drinking the blood of innocents.<br /> <br /> For the Masquerade, hunters are both the price one pays for defying it and a handy mechanism for aiding it. Those Kindred who are too sloppy tend to attract hunters. Those Kindred then either succeed in eliminating the threat, or get eliminated themselves (and are thus removed from the population). Some Kindred even exploit hunters in this capacity, as part of a <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/XanatosGambit\" target=\"_blank\">Xanatos Gambit</a>. Either the hunters or the sloppy (or inconvenient) licks get killed - maybe even both - so the manipulator always wins. That is, so long as they are careful, and don't let the hunter problem get too large. The Masquerade exists for a reason.<br /> <br /> In the Sabbat especially, it's probably seen as a natural outcome, if a pack is so incautious they attract hunters. They were being stupid, and thus deserved to die. The decentralized nature of the sect works in their favor in this situation, since rarely can a hunter group trace other packs after killing one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":6156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","user":"Bluecho","date":". 04-13-2017, 05:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T03:27:43-07:00","id":1077613,"title":"","content":"So in most cases, Technocracy don't need to intervene at all, either directly or indirectly, even in the sect's centre of power such as Mexico City? And significant portion of wod's crimes are perpetrated by hemophages instead of human criminals?<br /> <br /> Do vampires have any knowledge regarding mage society? And how they think about hunters, lupines, ghosts and other supernatural denizens?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11780,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11780-posthumanity","user":"Posthumanity","date":". 04-13-2017, 06:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11780-posthumanity","name":"Posthumanity","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T03:36:07-07:00","id":1077615,"title":"","content":"I'm starting to get the feeling you really don't know much about vampire the masquerade....<br /> <br /> 1.If you want them to in your chronicle, sure. Remember though, the technocracy game plan is to &quot;win&quot; the ascension war against the traditions first, THEN deal with everything else that goes bump in the night. The conventions simply don't have enough man power or resources to fight a two front war.<br /> <br /> 2. No that's just silly, sabbat tend to hide out In rough areas because it helps them go unnoticed.<br /> <br /> The tremere might because the clan sprang from them, but that's only the old elders. It's probably on par with vampires having knowledge about werewolves or fairies. <br /> <br /> Re: Hunters, how do you feel about someone who would break into your house and kill you in your sleep? Granted you could always try to get them to go after a rival....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13009,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","user":"BurritoMage","date":". 04-13-2017, 06:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T10:54:27-07:00","id":1077798,"title":"","content":"I suspect in genuine terms even during open warfare, the Cam and Sabbat don't lose much in the way of &quot;resources&quot; or &quot;casualties.&quot; Neonate deaths are basically irrelevant to the elders running the show.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BurritoMage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1077512-what-is-modus-operandi-of-nwo-against-vampires?p=1077583#post1077583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yep, elders still remember the burning times. Packs that can't keep it in their pants and think it's 30 days of night every night.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is particularly apt reference, as the comics version of 30 Days is a great example of the Sabbat's policy regarding the Masquerade (the movie makes some changes): There's no official policy, but the elders would be horrified and furious if a pack actually acted like there wasn't a policy. When the Sabbat says they don't follow the Masquerade, it's a political stance, not a sincere gameplan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i> I attack people with giant insects both </i>on <i>and </i>off <i>the court.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","name":"Five Eyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"395"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-23T05:58:06-07:00","id":1082569,"title":"","content":"depends on how far the vamps go of course. techies still wrecked the Mexico city in one plotline. and damn, was that glorious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-23T11:27:02-07:00","id":1082718,"title":"","content":"Simple.<br /> <br /> Observe and exterminate the most depraved leeches case-by-case. Or flag them to the Camarilla.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","name":"Numinous","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-23T11:38:53-07:00","id":1082723,"title":"","content":"In general Vampires (even the Sabbat) tend to police themselves. While the Sabbat talks a big game about how they don't follow the Masquerade, in truth most of them do, because they don't want to attract hunters (or groups rather like the NWO). For the most part, Sabbat vampires figure they'll keep their heads down now, until the Camarilla is defeated and then they can do whatever they want. But for now, their decision not to be too blatant is an important tactical one, and any vampires who don't understand that get dealt with. <br /> <br /> If a vampire or a pack goes truly overboard, the NWO might intervene, but more likely before the NWO gets around to it, other vampires will have already taken care of the problem. The NWO or other technocratic agents will show up at the rogue vampire's haven to take him down, and they'll find the haven is already on fire and the vampire dead. Vampire society, even the Sabbat, are probably even more invested in keeping their true nature a secret from the public than even the NWO is.<br /> <br /> So in those cases where the NWO does need to get involved, things have probably already spiraled out of control and that Camarilla or Sabbat's initial response to the Masquerade violations failed big time, such that an outside group like the NWO finds itself having to deal with the situation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-23T12:03:42-07:00","id":1082729,"title":"","content":"Using mortal hunters as proxies is a pretty textbook vampire move for dealing with their enemies and for serial masquerade problems that avoid/evade punishment. Stands to reason that the NWO would play the same game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-23T12:31:32-07:00","id":1082738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1077512-what-is-modus-operandi-of-nwo-against-vampires?p=1082729#post1082729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Using mortal hunters as proxies is a pretty textbook vampire move for dealing with their enemies and for serial masquerade problems that avoid/evade punishment. Stands to reason that the NWO would play the same game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed. Some NWO Operatives give intel or aids to mortal and Imbued Hunters. They also continuously feed other sects' movements to Camarilla. However, I suspect they are not above to take more direct measure when things spinning out of control.<br /> <br /> According to the Syndicate CB,<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> With the younger or more rebellious of their kind, though, that\u2019s best left to other Conventions to exterminate. Not that we can\u2019t, but our Enforcers are better served protecting the Bottom Line. </div> </div> </div>Obviously, 'other Conventions' include NWO. Though I think Syndicate would prefer Iteration X or Progenitors to perform cleanup operation.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","name":"Numinous","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-23T13:24:39-07:00","id":1082754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1077512-what-is-modus-operandi-of-nwo-against-vampires?p=1077545#post1077545\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Indeed, it's easier for them to rock the Consensus, on account of them being mysteriously immune to Paradox and Disbelief (and, unlike the changing breeds, have no built-in mechanism for covering their tracks). But it's for that same reason - and their predatory unlifestyle - that Vampires also have the greatest incentive to <i>police themselves</i> when it comes to keeping the secret from mortals. They do the Technocracy's job for them, for both themselves and for other supernatural weirdness. The Kindred are kind enough to see to their own secrecy, leaving the Union free to handle less accommodating reality deviants.<br /> <br /> What's more, they're damn good at it. Memory alteration is one of the most common powers available to Vampires, and they can enslave people with their addictive blood if that doesn't take. Point being, while they can be an enormous threat to the Consensus, they have just as much a vested interest in keeping it as the Technocracy does, and are capable of doing so.<br /> <br /> They're SO capable of hiding, in fact, that even the Technocracy is woefully ignorant of just how extensive the hemophage problem really is. The Union assumes vampires are rare. If they knew the full scope of the Kindred population, they'd probably take them far more seriously.</div> </div> </div> </div>Err no. They know the full extent of the Kindred population in any major population center. The guide to the Technocracy goes so far as to laugh at the Vampires for being too old school and focusing too much on the human element. It doesn't matter how many policemen you brainwash or mindwipe if the Union can scan the city and pick out the people who aren't actually alive.<br /> <br /> The reason why they don't care is because they're unaware of just how powerful older generation vampires can be. Or they were up until Operation Ragnarok.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-23T13:43:27-07:00","id":1082758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1077512-what-is-modus-operandi-of-nwo-against-vampires?p=1082754#post1082754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Err no. They know the full extent of the Kindred population in any major population center. The guide to the Technocracy goes so far as to laugh at the Vampires for being too old school and focusing too much on the human element. It doesn't matter how many policemen you brainwash or mindwipe if the Union can scan the city and pick out the people who aren't actually alive.<br /> <br /> The reason why they don't care is because they're unaware of just how powerful older generation vampires can be. Or they were up until Operation Ragnarok.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I have a grievance at revised CB, it is Union's party line and general perspective against vampires has not been changed much, despite of Operation Ragnarok and Dimensional Anomaly. It is only reasonable that after the Reorganization, Union has to deactivate Pogrom and allying with every other faction and go all-out war against vampires with every available asset, including make existence of vampire public.<br /> <br /> No matter vampires brainwashing power, Union simply broadcasts credible evidence across every single media and activates global mobilization.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4173,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","user":"Numinous","date":". 04-23-2017, 05:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","name":"Numinous","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-23T13:48:07-07:00","id":1082759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Numinous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1077512-what-is-modus-operandi-of-nwo-against-vampires?p=1082758#post1082758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I have a grievance at revised CB, it is Union's party line and general perspective against vampires has not been changed much, despite of Operation Ragnarok and Dimensional Anomaly.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's because no one can come to a definite conclusion as to what climbed out of the Indian Ocean and necessitated operation Ragnarok. It could have been a lot of things from a PC perspective and quite frankly I like it that way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-23T13:49:28-07:00","id":1082761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BurritoMage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1077512-what-is-modus-operandi-of-nwo-against-vampires?p=1082759#post1082759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's because no one can come to a definite conclusion as to what climbed out of the Indian Ocean and necessitated operation Ragnarok. It could have been a lot of things from a PC perspective and quite frankly I like it that way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Void Engineers know. And their hatred against vampires burns bright.<br /> <br /> And of course, NWO is well aware of what Zapathasura truly is. In fact, they know vampire prophecies and Book of Nod.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The rumormongering among the vampires of an end of days, of a time when their legends rise up, has come and passed without incident. To be honest, that comes as a bit of a surprise, as the Statisticians calculated catastrophe in line with their prophecies. </div> </div> </div>So lack of knowledge is no excuse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4173,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","user":"Numinous","date":". 04-23-2017, 04:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","name":"Numinous","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-23T14:34:16-07:00","id":1082770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Numinous</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I have a grievance at revised CB, it is Union's party line and general perspective against vampires has not been changed much, despite of Operation Ragnarok and Dimensional Anomaly. It is only reasonable that after the Reorganization, Union has to deactivate Pogrom and allying with every other faction and go all-out war against vampires with every available asset, including make existence of vampire public.<br /> <br /> No matter vampires brainwashing power, Union simply broadcasts credible evidence across every single media and activates global mobilization.</div> </div> </div> </div>I fell your pain, because vampires, in crossover, seem more dangerous than the Traditions.<br /> <br /> With allying with every other faction (exept the Nephandi) I agree, albeit the other factions are kind of a mess. The Traditons haven't a partyline about what to do with vampires,and while most agree they're a plage that has to be eradicated, they think the same of Technocrats (hey, vampires usually don't go out of their way to crush Traditionalist ambitions). The Disparate are worse, and Hollow Ones sometimes befriend the leeches. Marauders speak for themselves. It's unlikely the Union can convince these egocentric and arrogant people to join unless the vampiric threat it's obvious. But it would worth a try.<br /> <br /> With activating global movilization, on the other hand, I have to quote the Men in Black themselves:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>imdb, Men in Black</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <a href=\"http://www.imdb.com/name/nm0000169/?ref_=tt_trv_qu\" target=\"_blank\">Kay</a>: We do not discharge our weapons in view of the public!<br /> <a href=\"http://www.imdb.com/name/nm0000226/?ref_=tt_trv_qu\" target=\"_blank\">Jay</a>: Man, we ain't got time for this cover-up bullshit! I don't know whether or not you've forgotten, but there's an Arquillian Battle Cruiser that's about to...<br /> <a href=\"http://www.imdb.com/name/nm0000169/?ref_=tt_trv_qu\" target=\"_blank\">Kay</a>: There's always an Arquillian Battle Cruiser, or a Corillian Death Ray, or an intergalactic plague that is about to wipe out all life on this miserable little planet, and the only way these people can get on with their happy lives is that they DO NOT KNOW ABOUT IT!<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>It's a bad idea to end the masquerade that the NWO had been enforcing so carefully for so long. The reason it exists it's to better control the Consensus, to make the masses believe they live in a world ruled by humans and human choices. the mass hysteria caused by a sudden revelation of vampires it's not something the NWO wants. Doing so it's only acceptable if the Technocracy acknowledges that they can't handle the problem without discretion, and that's something they will never do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 04-23-2017, 05:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-23T14:55:37-07:00","id":1082777,"title":"","content":"Don't forget that the Vampires are quite literally nothing short of vermin to the Technocracy. In one of the books, a mage made a virus to wipe out large swaths of vampires that fed on those with the blood and it caused a bunch of deaths. They had to cured it after the power vacuum began to form. I believe it was the Verbena book. Now you can imagine if the Technocrats actually wanted to wipe out the Vampires, they could very much do so but they don't cause it's more work which affects the Bottom Line. Syndicate Mages hate having their numbers messed with and remember, the Syndicate feed the rest of the Technocracy more or less. Besides, Camarilla vampires also like money, which makes for better profits for the Syndicate. Hell Elders are basically on terms of Syndicate Mages when it comes to wanting to make more money.<br /> <br /> But yeah, vermin aren't worth the time nor the effort to police. As a species, we could easily wipe out mosquitoes but we haven't done so yet because it's not worth the effort. Technocracy is trying to protect Humanity as a whole, not individuals. If some Technocrat has some anger to vent, they'd probably just go wipe out a vampire nest, but other than that they pass equipment and information to the Hunters/Templars/Traditions/Werewolves/Camarilla and let them take care of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1VN49Y7tH2ZV0l7Hx65RWX1ez-Q9Lst-8ZTyTJeCTpxM/\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerer 20th</a> homebrew and my update to <a href=\"http://immortalthegathering.blogspot.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Highlander: the Gathering</a> for 20th Anniversary edition.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2414-theoutlander523","name":"theoutlander523","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-23T15:04:49-07:00","id":1082781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>theoutlander523</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1077512-what-is-modus-operandi-of-nwo-against-vampires?p=1082777#post1082777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't forget that the Vampires are quite literally nothing short of vermin to the Technocracy. In one of the books, a mage made a virus to wipe out large swaths of vampires that fed on those with the blood and it caused a bunch of deaths. They had to cured it after the power vacuum began to form. I believe it was the Verbena book. Now you can imagine if the Technocrats actually wanted to wipe out the Vampires, they could very much do so but they don't cause it's more work which affects the Bottom Line. Syndicate Mages hate having their numbers messed with and remember, the Syndicate feed the rest of the Technocracy more or less. Besides, Camarilla vampires also like money, which makes for better profits for the Syndicate. Hell Elders are basically on terms of Syndicate Mages when it comes to wanting to make more money.<br /> <br /> But yeah, vermin aren't worth the time nor the effort to police. As a species, we could easily wipe out mosquitoes but we haven't done so yet because it's not worth the effort. Technocracy is trying to protect Humanity as a whole, not individuals. If some Technocrat has some anger to vent, they'd probably just go wipe out a vampire nest, but other than that they pass equipment and information to the Hunters/Templars/Traditions/Werewolves/Camarilla and let them take care of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>As of Revised, in absence of a pogrom to pursue, Iteration X has made it a priority to kill vampires. Because they apparently can't live without an enemy to crush.<br /> <br /> In some ways, Iteration X's characterization reminds me of the D&amp;D-esque murderhobo. Cut away the 'human' parts that give them character in order to gain mechanical advantages. Murder anything that opposes them even tangentially. Refer to the less warmongering conventions as cowards barely worthy of their partnership.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-23T15:09:34-07:00","id":1082783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1077512-what-is-modus-operandi-of-nwo-against-vampires?p=1082781#post1082781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As of Revised, in absence of a pogrom to pursue, Iteration X has made it a priority to kill vampires. Because they apparently can't live without an enemy to crush.<br /> <br /> In some ways, Iteration X's characterization reminds me of the D&amp;D-esque murderhobo. Cut away the 'human' parts that give them character in order to gain mechanical advantages. Murder anything that opposes them even tangentially. Refer to the less warmongering conventions as cowards barely worthy of their partnership.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unfortunately we never got an It-X 2011 Convention book so the degree to how correct that is now is a bit up in the air. Never understood why they just don't hunt spirits though, always lots of spirits to kill. You know, like the Bane ones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1VN49Y7tH2ZV0l7Hx65RWX1ez-Q9Lst-8ZTyTJeCTpxM/\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerer 20th</a> homebrew and my update to <a href=\"http://immortalthegathering.blogspot.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Highlander: the Gathering</a> for 20th Anniversary edition.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2414-theoutlander523","name":"theoutlander523","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-23T15:17:02-07:00","id":1082784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>theoutlander523</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1077512-what-is-modus-operandi-of-nwo-against-vampires?p=1082783#post1082783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Unfortunately we never got an It-X 2011 Convention book so the degree to how correct that is now is a bit up in the air. Never understood why they just don't hunt spirits though, always lots of spirits to kill. You know, like the Bane ones.</div> </div> </div> </div>They don't view them as spirits in the shamanic sense but as aliens or extra dimensional entities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-23T15:28:20-07:00","id":1082787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BurritoMage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1077512-what-is-modus-operandi-of-nwo-against-vampires?p=1082784#post1082784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They don't view them as spirits in the shamanic sense but as aliens or extra dimensional entities.</div> </div> </div> </div>Never said they didn't. Just saying that there's always spirits to kill.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1VN49Y7tH2ZV0l7Hx65RWX1ez-Q9Lst-8ZTyTJeCTpxM/\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerer 20th</a> homebrew and my update to <a href=\"http://immortalthegathering.blogspot.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Highlander: the Gathering</a> for 20th Anniversary edition.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2414-theoutlander523","name":"theoutlander523","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-23T15:28:58-07:00","id":1082788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>theoutlander523</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Never understood why they just don't hunt spirits though, always lots of spirits to kill. You know, like the Bane ones.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because during the major part of their history they were under the control of the Computer. And, the Computer, being a spirit, decided that it was in its best interest to forbidde all ItX, with the possible exeption of his most devoted folowers that lived in Autochtonia, from developing powers to sense and battle spirits.<br /> The result it's ItX, even after been freed from the Computer by the Anomaly, having near zero users of Dimiesional Science, and from those who have it fewer would be aware of the Middle Umbra, and even less would aknowledge it's importance or even care.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 04-23-2017, 06:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-23T15:38:14-07:00","id":1082793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1077512-what-is-modus-operandi-of-nwo-against-vampires?p=1082788#post1082788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Because during the major part of their history they were under the control of the Computer. And, the Computer, being a spirit, decided that it was in its best interest to forbidde all ItX, with the possible exeption of his most devoted folowers that lived in Autochtonia, from developing powers to sense and battle spirits.<br /> The result it's ItX, even after been freed from the Computer by the Anomaly, having near zero users of Dimiesional Science, and from those who have it fewer would be aware of the Middle Umbra, and even less would aknowledge it's importance or even care.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't need to know DS in order to hunt spirits. They're all over the damn place, fomori are almost as much of a pest as Vampires according to Werewolf. Just send a few hitmarks down the street and watch them kill people possessed by &quot;aliens&quot; with their bare hands.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1VN49Y7tH2ZV0l7Hx65RWX1ez-Q9Lst-8ZTyTJeCTpxM/\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerer 20th</a> homebrew and my update to <a href=\"http://immortalthegathering.blogspot.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Highlander: the Gathering</a> for 20th Anniversary edition.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2414-theoutlander523","name":"theoutlander523","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-23T16:35:38-07:00","id":1082819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1077512-what-is-modus-operandi-of-nwo-against-vampires?p=1082754#post1082754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Err no. They know the full extent of the Kindred population in any major population center. The guide to the Technocracy goes so far as to laugh at the Vampires for being too old school and focusing too much on the human element. It doesn't matter how many policemen you brainwash or mindwipe if the Union can scan the city and pick out the people who aren't actually alive.<br /> <br /> The reason why they don't care is because they're unaware of just how powerful older generation vampires can be. Or they were up until Operation Ragnarok.</div> </div> </div> </div>Remember, the Guide to the Technocracy is written <i>from the perspective</i> of the Technocracy. They <i>think</i> they know the full extent of the vampire population.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-23T16:37:14-07:00","id":1082822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Numinous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1077512-what-is-modus-operandi-of-nwo-against-vampires?p=1082758#post1082758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No matter vampires brainwashing power, Union simply broadcasts credible evidence across every single media and activates global mobilization.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem with that scenario is it necessitates the Technocracy themselves coming out the shadows. They don't want that. It only ends badly for them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-23T16:45:30-07:00","id":1082823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>theoutlander523</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't need to know DS in order to hunt spirits. They're all over the damn place, fomori are almost as much of a pest as Vampires according to Werewolf. Just send a few hitmarks down the street and watch them kill people possessed by &quot;aliens&quot; with their bare hands.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, they surely do that. If it moves and has supernatural power you can be sure there's a ItX machine that wants to make a rug with it. But they don't know it's an alien.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Remember, the Guide to the Technocracy is written <i>from the perspective</i> of the Technocracy. They <i>think</i> they know the full extent of the vampire population.</div> </div> </div> </div>And what it's what they don't know that could make for a better case to hunt vampires than what they already know?<br /> <br /> One could make a case that they don't know that there's supposed to be eleven Ravnos more, but they've got the Book of Nod, so they should do as any paranoid organization would do, and at least entertain the possibility (at least in the high ranks). They know that the Sabbat likes to kill humans in the most horrifying fashion, and that the Camarilla has such a great control of the economical system that they can't be easily eradicated. Do you really need anything more?, When was the last time the Traditions did something that's remotely on the level of what the Technocracy knows that vampires do or can do?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 04-23-2017, 07:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-23T17:01:18-07:00","id":1082832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1077512-what-is-modus-operandi-of-nwo-against-vampires?p=1082823#post1082823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And what it's what they don't know that could make for a better case to hunt vampires than what they already know?<br /> <br /> One could make a case that they don't know that there's supposed to be eleven Ravnos more, but they've got the Book of Nod, so they should do as any paranoid organization would do, and at least entertain the possibility (at least in the high ranks). They know that the Sabbat likes to kill humans in the most horrifying fashion, and that the Camarilla has such a great control of the economical system that they can't be easily eradicated. Do you really need anything more?, When was the last time the Traditions did something that's remotely on the level of what the Technocracy knows that vampires do or can do?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh I'm not arguing with that, just that the Technocracy doesn't have the level of perfect intelligence on the problem that a lot of them think they do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-23T23:49:11-07:00","id":1082914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1077512-what-is-modus-operandi-of-nwo-against-vampires?p=1082822#post1082822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem with that scenario is it necessitates the Technocracy themselves coming out the shadows. They don't want that. It only ends badly for them.</div> </div> </div> </div>What do you mean? Why it ends badly for the Technocracy? If humanity know existence of <i>both </i>vampires and the Technocracy, they will side with the latter. And it does not seem likely that the Technocracy has to come out the shadows to broadcast existential threat of bloodsucking leeches.<br /> <br /> And Consensus is to be damned. If the Union is forced to choose between Consensus and the world, they will gladly choose the world. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","name":"Numinous","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T00:06:58-07:00","id":1082920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1077512-what-is-modus-operandi-of-nwo-against-vampires?p=1082832#post1082832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh I'm not arguing with that, just that the Technocracy doesn't have the level of perfect intelligence on the problem that a lot of them think they do.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Union does not need to know full extent of the leech population. A dozen or so Ravnos and Sabbat's rampaging is perfect clause to declare total war against bloodsuckers. And while the Union does not have <i>exact </i>number, they know there are 'countless leeches' in 'every major population center'. They are fully aware of each vampire sect, clan, bloodline and its traits, proclivities, characteristics, assets, influence and modus operandi. They already have more than enough knowledge to devise sound, comprehensive strategy to scour the leeches from face of the Earth. <br /> <br /> I still cannot help to wonder why the Union's archenemy is the Tradition. Vampires are literally <i>everything </i>original OoR vowed to eradicate. You can also assure that vampires are crystalization of everything the Union is opposing. Vampires are potentially more dangerous than <i>every other supernatural threat combined</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","name":"Numinous","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T03:28:15-07:00","id":1082955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Numinous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1077512-what-is-modus-operandi-of-nwo-against-vampires?p=1082914#post1082914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do you mean? Why it ends badly for the Technocracy? If humanity know existence of <i>both </i>vampires and the Technocracy, they will side with the latter. And it does not seem likely that the Technocracy has to come out the shadows to broadcast existential threat of bloodsucking leeches.<br /> <br /> And Consensus is to be damned. If the Union is forced to choose between Consensus and the world, they will gladly choose the world.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>To most Technocrats. The Consensus IS the world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T04:55:19-07:00","id":1082970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Numinous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1077512-what-is-modus-operandi-of-nwo-against-vampires?p=1082920#post1082920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They are fully aware of each vampire sect, clan, bloodline and its traits, proclivities, characteristics, assets, influence and modus operandi.</div> </div> </div> </div>[Citation Needed]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T07:13:04-07:00","id":1083000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Numinous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1077512-what-is-modus-operandi-of-nwo-against-vampires?p=1082914#post1082914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do you mean? Why it ends badly for the Technocracy? If humanity know existence of <i>both </i>vampires and the Technocracy, they will side with the latter. And it does not seem likely that the Technocracy has to come out the shadows to broadcast existential threat of bloodsucking leeches.<br /> <br /> And Consensus is to be damned. If the Union is forced to choose between Consensus and the world, they will gladly choose the world.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Which is obviously why the Technocracy is already completely open about its existence and activities, ruling publicly as the benevolent priest-kings they are, dispensing Olympian fire to the masses to illuminate all the dark places that there is no longer any need for.<br /> <br /> Except no. The Technocracy lives in the shadows just like the vampires they claim to despise, and for much the same reason. The Technocracy is only able to rule so long as humanity isn't aware they are being ruled.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T07:40:21-07:00","id":1083007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1077512-what-is-modus-operandi-of-nwo-against-vampires?p=1083000#post1083000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which is obviously why the Technocracy is already completely open about its existence and activities, ruling publicly as the benevolent priest-kings they are, dispensing Olympian fire to the masses to illuminate all the dark places that there is no longer any need for.<br /> <br /> Except no. The Technocracy lives in the shadows just like the vampires they claim to despise, and for much the same reason. The Technocracy is only able to rule so long as humanity isn't aware they are being ruled.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Technocracy doesn't live in the shadows at all. It's just opaque on all but the surface levels. Just like the real government.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T08:32:38-07:00","id":1083025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1077512-what-is-modus-operandi-of-nwo-against-vampires?p=1083000#post1083000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which is obviously why the Technocracy is already completely open about its existence and activities, ruling publicly as the benevolent priest-kings they are, dispensing Olympian fire to the masses to illuminate all the dark places that there is no longer any need for.<br /> <br /> Except no. The Technocracy lives in the shadows just like the vampires they claim to despise, and for much the same reason. The Technocracy is only able to rule so long as humanity isn't aware they are being ruled.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know how the Technocracy recruits, right? They don't live in shadow like the vampires. They <i>are </i>government. They <i>are </i>corporation. They <i>are </i>academia. They <i>are </i>science community. They <i>are</i> mass media. They <i>are </i>military, and so on. Most Technocrats operate in daylight. They merely have another, 'true' identity. Just like RW special agencies.<br /> <br /> Sleepers work for the Technocracy while are not aware of its 'true' nature, just like Pentex. Technocracy is always acting openly on the surface level. Always.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","name":"Numinous","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T08:42:15-07:00","id":1083029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1077512-what-is-modus-operandi-of-nwo-against-vampires?p=1082970#post1082970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> [Citation Needed]</div> </div> </div> </div>They know Sabbat and other sects and how they are operating. They know each sect's feudal structure and society. They <i>know </i>Tremere. They <i>know </i>thaumaturgy and arguing about why it does not violate reality. They <i>know </i>how Tremere was corrupted. They <i>deal with </i>vampire in friendly term, even though vampires are woefully blind of existence of the Syndicate, let alone the Technocracy. They infiltrate in vampire society and feed information in various sects and parties. They <i>research </i>and <i>categorize </i>every known type of vampire.<br /> <br /> Then, it is only probable the Technocracy <i>know </i>each sect and clan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4173,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","user":"Numinous","date":". 04-24-2017, 02:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","name":"Numinous","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T09:12:14-07:00","id":1083041,"title":"","content":"Lets be clear. At <i>worst</i>, even if existence of Technocracy is made public, it simply proves crack conspiracy theorists claim of &quot;shadow government&quot; or &quot;New World Order&quot;. And it is the worst case scenario.<br /> <br /> And if the public suddenly possess complete knowledge of <i>vampire </i>shadow government malevolent literal bloodsucking conspiracy(Camarilla), world-wide psychopathic malefic criminal bloodsucking gangs(Sabbat), deviant, deranged, corrupt cannibal bloodsucking necromancy-incest-bankers(Giovanni, and they are deviant in every imaginable way), diabolic bloodsucking opium apocalypse cultists of satan(FoS and Baali) and so on? How do you think humanity will react between benevolent human government conspiracy and pure, unadulterated distillation of the every single worst negative meme, trope, nightmare and conspiracy theory of the vampires?<br /> <br /> Technocracy does not reveal its existence public because of <i>simple convenience</i>. For instance, thanks to Dimensional Anomaly. Syndicate's operational cover in UN, World Bank, IMF, WTO, FRS, ECB and other such global-scale organizations has been blown out. It exposed &quot;shadow financiers&quot; and &quot;back-room dealing&quot; who design, shape and guide world economy. The result? World-wide anti-globalization campaigns. Noting more. Vampires live and operate in shadow for their own <i>damned undead lives</i>.<br /> <br /> Then, let's see how Imbued Hunters view and react to the Technocracy. It has been explicitly stated several times over there is no hostilities between them and the Technocracy provides intel, help and aids for them time to time. Even if they feel Technocracy is 'tainted' as other mages, they do not automatically react 'kill on sight or track down until it stop twitch' like the vampires. They assume Technocrats are some types of secret government agents, military, corporate tycoons, government-sponsored scientists and so on. And these are <i>exactly </i>their cover identities in the Sleeper world. Mortal hunters are even more easily co-opted.<br /> <br /> Inquisition? They do not know Technocracy. In fact, very few hunters know, or see, even glimpse of the vast, monolithic conspiracy constantly observing, categorizing, informing, and (sometimes) backing them. If they know something <i>at all</i>.<br /> <br /> And how they react against vampires...that is everyone's guess. It would be sufficient safe to say hunters and Inquisition 'main designated enemies' are vampires and they hunts down other supernatural case by case scenarios. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4173,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","user":"Numinous","date":". 04-24-2017, 12:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","name":"Numinous","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T09:16:27-07:00","id":1083044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Numinous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1077512-what-is-modus-operandi-of-nwo-against-vampires?p=1083041#post1083041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lets be clear. At <i>worst</i>, even if existence of Technocracy is made public, it simply proves crack conspiracy theorists claim of &quot;shadow government&quot; or &quot;New World Order&quot;. And it is the worst scenario.<br /> <br /> And if the public suddenly possess <i>vampire </i>shadow government malevolent conspiracy(Camarilla), world-wide psychopathic malefic criminal gangs(Sabbat), deviant, deranged, corrupt cannibal bankers(Giovanni, and they are deviant in every imaginable way), diabolic cultists(FoS and Baali) and so on? How do you think humanity will react between benevolent human government conspiracy and pure, unadulterated distillation of the every single worst meme, trope and conspiracy theory of the vampires?<br /> <br /> Technocracy does not reveal its existence public because of <i>simple convenience</i>. For instance, thanks to Dimensional Anomaly. Syndicate's operational cover in UN, World Bank, IMF, WTO, FRS, ECB and other such global-scale organizations has been blown out. It exposed &quot;shadow financiers&quot; and &quot;back-room dealing&quot; who design, shape and guide world economy. The result? World-wide anti-globalization campaigns. Noting more. Vampires live and operate in shadow for their own <i>damned undead lives</i>.<br /> <br /> Then, let's see how Imbued Hunters view and react against Technocracy. It has been explicitly stated several times over there is no hostilities between them and the Technocracy provides intel, help and aids for them time to time. Even if they feel Technocracy is 'tainted' as other mages, they do not automatically react 'kill on sight or track down until it stop twitch' like the vampires. They assume Technocrats are some types of secret government agents, military, corporate tycoons, government-sponsored scientists and so on. And these are <i>exactly </i>their cover identities in the Sleeper world. Mortal hunters are even more easily co-opted.<br /> <br /> Inquisition? They do not know Technocracy. In fact, very few hunters know, or see, even glimpse of the vast, monolithic conspiracy constantly observing, categorizing, informing, and (sometimes) backing them. If they know something <i>at all</i>.<br /> <br /> And how they react against vampires...that is everyone's guess. It would be sufficient safe to say hunters and Inquisition 'main designated enemies' are vampires and they hunts down other supernatural case by case scenarios. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I suspect that most of the &quot;secrecy&quot; of the Technocracy in other games has far more to do with Mage being so out there that any references to its antagonist groups are minimized to the point of their might as well being fringe cults that have nothing to do with Mage. Because, seriously, by the standards of other games, Mage is super out there, and it helps for the cohesiveness of the other settings to ignore the existence of the outlier rather than try to detail each and every little reaction that wouldn't even make sense outside of Mage's cosmology.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T10:11:51-07:00","id":1083068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1077512-what-is-modus-operandi-of-nwo-against-vampires?p=1083007#post1083007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Technocracy doesn't live in the shadows at all. It's just opaque on all but the surface levels. Just like the real government.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a difference between a visible government with varying degrees of transparency throughout and an entirely opaque shadow government that nobody even knows exists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T10:16:38-07:00","id":1083071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1077512-what-is-modus-operandi-of-nwo-against-vampires?p=1083044#post1083044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I suspect that most of the &quot;secrecy&quot; of the Technocracy in other games has far more to do with Mage being so out there that any references to its antagonist groups are minimized to the point of their might as well being fringe cults that have nothing to do with Mage. Because, seriously, by the standards of other games, Mage is super out there, and it helps for the cohesiveness of the other settings to ignore the existence of the outlier rather than try to detail each and every little reaction that wouldn't even make sense outside of Mage's cosmology.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed. If the Technocracy is as powerful, colossal and far-reaching as Mage portrays it, there is no way other &quot;major&quot; supernaturals are utterly blind of its very existence while Technocracy collects extensive(and mostly accurate) intelligence regarding its antagonists.<br /> <br /> This would be applied equally true to the Pentex, Camarilla and Garou Nation. If they are as powerful as their own lines' portrayal, every other supernatural faction has to <i>know </i>their existence and activities. However, werewolves are considering vampires as mere abominable vermin and aberrant distraction. In turn, Camarilla is woefully ignorant of <i>both </i>the Pentex and Garou Nation. I have never seen &quot;Pentex&quot; or &quot;Glass Walkers/Silver Fangs, et cetra&quot; in Vampire books. Hell, vampires think city dwelling lupines were driven to extinct and they have exterminated every single lupine intruder, while in WtA book, many werewolf sects are in city and <i>most </i>werewolves are city-dwellers. Finally, Pentex is completely blind about both the vampire and the mage. Pentex has to know something about Technocracy. According to Mage lore, Technocracy is Pentex's founder, after all. And they have to routinely deal with government, corporate world, science community, mass media, private security and military, and so on. And they have to compete with vampires and the Technocracy for world dominance if those organizations are existing in the same form and status. However Pentex books never, ever mention anything neither the Technocracy nor the vampires, except a brief comment about some Sabbat Wyrm cults, and even that is come from BSD's collective mouth.<br /> <br /> It is one of many reasons why I regard each line is basically a parallel universe, and if we borrow Technocracy's term, &quot;Everett Volumes&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4173,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","user":"Numinous","date":". 04-24-2017, 01:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","name":"Numinous","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T10:18:29-07:00","id":1083074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Numinous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1077512-what-is-modus-operandi-of-nwo-against-vampires?p=1083025#post1083025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know how the Technocracy recruits, right? They don't live in shadow like the vampires. They <i>are </i>government. They <i>are </i>corporation. They <i>are </i>academia. They <i>are </i>science community. They <i>are</i> mass media. They <i>are </i>military, and so on. Most Technocrats operate in daylight. They merely have another, 'true' identity. Just like RW special agencies.<br /> <br /> Sleepers work for the Technocracy while are not aware of its 'true' nature, just like Pentex. Technocracy is always acting openly on the surface level. Always.</div> </div> </div> </div>Vampires also have embedded recruits everywhere, they just have to be more careful about their profile. Sleepers also work for vampires without being aware of their true nature. If all we're doing is measuring influence then vampires are also always acting openly on the surface level. Always.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T10:32:14-07:00","id":1083078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Numinous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1077512-what-is-modus-operandi-of-nwo-against-vampires?p=1083071#post1083071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Indeed. If the Technocracy is as powerful, colossal and far-reaching as Mage portrays it, there is no way other &quot;major&quot; supernaturals are utterly blind of its very existence while Technocracy collects extensive(and mostly accurate) intelligence regarding its antagonists.<br /> <br /> This would be applied equally well to the Pentex, Camarilla and Garou Nation. If they are as powerful as their own lines' portrayal, every other supernatural faction has to <i>know </i>their existence and activities. However, werewolves are considering vampires as mere abominable vermin and aberrant distraction. In turn, Camarilla is woefully ignorant of <i>both </i>the Pentex and Garou Nation. I have never seen &quot;Pentex&quot; or &quot;Glass Walkers/Silver Fangs, et cetra&quot; in Vampire books.</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically, &quot;Pentex&quot; shouldn't even be thrown around willy-nilly in Werewolf, since it's an obscured holding company that has a bunch of much, much more prominent subsidiaries under its umbrella. Those do get name-dropped in other games, so it muddies the water.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Hell, vampires think city dwelling lupines were driven to extinct and they have exterminated every single lupine intruder, while in WtA book, many werewolf sects are in city and <i>most </i>werewolves are city-dwellers. </div> </div> </div>No, actually, most Garou are still not in the city. The two largest tribes do tend to live in urban areas, but they catch flak about it from more rural septs. In any case, vampires also don't know that spirits exist, for the most part, which is decidedly to the advantage of the Garou and Fera.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Finally, Pentex is completely blind about both the vampire and the mage. </div> </div> </div>Probably not, since someone keeps cramming the stars of other games into leadership positions somewhere, and Avalon toys is headed by a soundly warped SoE.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Pentex has to know something about Technocracy. According to Mage lore, Technocracy is Pentex's founder, after all. </div> </div> </div>Which book claims that? Honest question.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And they have to routinely deal with government, corporate world, science community, mass media, private security and military, and so on. However Pentex books never, ever mention anything about the Technocracy.<br /> <br /> It is one of many reasons why I deem each line is basically a parallel universe, and if we borrow Technocracy's term, &quot;Everett Volumes&quot; </div> </div> </div>Some of them are further away than others. If all the lines but Mage are planets in this solar system, Mage is out in the Oort cloud, at the very closest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T10:34:02-07:00","id":1083080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Numinous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1077512-what-is-modus-operandi-of-nwo-against-vampires?p=1083041#post1083041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lets be clear. At <i>worst</i>, even if existence of Technocracy is made public, it simply proves crack conspiracy theorists claim of &quot;shadow government&quot; or &quot;New World Order&quot;. And it is the worst case scenario.</div> </div> </div> </div>And I'm sure that everyone is going to be completely cool with that and its going to work out for the Technocracy just fine. Hey, if they're really hellbent on revealing themselves to the world to stop this terrible undead menace then I fully support this move. I couldn't be happier for them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T10:45:49-07:00","id":1083089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1077512-what-is-modus-operandi-of-nwo-against-vampires?p=1083078#post1083078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Technically, &quot;Pentex&quot; shouldn't even be thrown around willy-nilly in Werewolf, since it's an obscured holding company that has a bunch of much, much more prominent subsidiaries under its umbrella. Those do get name-dropped in other games, so it muddies the water.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is no small wonder werewolves even know &quot;Pentex&quot; as a coherent entity. And how those subsidiaries get their names dropped in other games? I have only seen SPD in Mage lines. It is a honest question - I'm really curious.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1077512-what-is-modus-operandi-of-nwo-against-vampires?p=1083078#post1083078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, actually, most Garou are still not in the city. The two largest tribes do tend to live in urban areas, but they catch flak about it from more rural septs. In any case, vampires also don't know that spirits exist, for the most part, which is decidedly to the advantage of the Garou and Fera.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Oops. My bad. Yeah, Garou and Fera is still more prominent in the wild and countryside. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1077512-what-is-modus-operandi-of-nwo-against-vampires?p=1083078#post1083078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Probably not, since someone keeps cramming the stars of other games into leadership positions somewhere, and Avalon toys is headed by a soundly warped SoE.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">That is mentioned in BoW. However, BoW also explicitly states Pentex does not really know anything about vampires and mages...and even their knowledge about werewolves is patchy at best, despite of its BSD presence. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1077512-what-is-modus-operandi-of-nwo-against-vampires?p=1083078#post1083078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which book claims that? Honest question.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">You have to read Syndicate books to know &quot;true&quot; crossover history of Pentex(damn, I really hate that crossover...). Pentex is child of North American Proctor House and Premium Oil. Syndicate merged the both corporations and baby Pentex was born. And then Syndicate founded SPD as its own internal R&amp;D division...<br /> <br /> Well, if you take crossover option, anyway. </span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4173,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","user":"Numinous","date":". 04-24-2017, 01:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","name":"Numinous","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T10:57:04-07:00","id":1083091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Numinous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1077512-what-is-modus-operandi-of-nwo-against-vampires?p=1083089#post1083089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is no small wonder werewolves even know &quot;Pentex&quot; as a coherent entity. And how those subsidiaries get their names dropped in other games? I have only seen SPD in Mage lines. It is a honest question - I'm really curious.</div> </div> </div> </div>You typically find them in references to fast food joint O'Tolley's, Tellus Games, or the like. It tends to show up more in the artwork than the text, though it could be getting muddled in my head.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">That is mentioned in BoW. However, BoW also explicitly states Pentex does not really know anything about vampires and mages...and even their knowledge about werewolves is patchy at best, despite of its BSD presence. </span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>BoW? Is this distinct from Book of the Wyrm/BotW?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">You have to read Syndicate books to know &quot;true&quot; crossover history of Pentex(damn, I really hate that crossover...). Pentex is child of North American Proctor House and Premium Oil. Syndicate merged the both corporations and baby Pentex was born. And then Syndicate founded SPD as its own internal R&amp;D division...<br /> <br /> Well, if you take crossover option, anyway. </span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>I knew about Premium Oil. It's listed as the primary cause or seed of what became Pentex in the rough timeline that the Werewolf Storyteller's Guide gave (the book that came with the Revised ST screen), since one of its early members had... a certain kind of help from beyond.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T11:14:08-07:00","id":1083096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1077512-what-is-modus-operandi-of-nwo-against-vampires?p=1083074#post1083074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampires also have embedded recruits everywhere, they just have to be more careful about their profile. Sleepers also work for vampires without being aware of their true nature. If all we're doing is measuring influence then vampires are also always acting openly on the surface level. Always.</div> </div> </div> </div>No. Vampires have embedded ghouls in select areas - in other worlds, positions can exert most handy influence over local city and protect their masters and provide masters' needs and check masters' rivals. <br /> Oh, wait, in case of Giovanni, they embed ghouls to support their necromancy researches and fund it.<br /> <br /> In personal, Vampires are always acting shadowy on the surface level. Always.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","name":"Numinous","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T11:16:25-07:00","id":1083098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1077512-what-is-modus-operandi-of-nwo-against-vampires?p=1083080#post1083080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I'm sure that everyone is going to be completely cool with that and its going to work out for the Technocracy just fine.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Of course</i> every living human being except Ghoul is going to be completely cool with that and its going to work out for the Technocracy just fine to combat apocalyptic undead menace pervading every facet and layer of society and walk of life.<br /> <br /> They probably even <i>admire </i>the shadow government hell-bent on utterly eradication of global undead menace living in their midst and preying upon them each and every night.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","name":"Numinous","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T11:23:54-07:00","id":1083101,"title":"","content":"&quot;Pentex's founder&quot; is a stretch.<br /> <br /> The Syndicate owned Proctor House (&quot;one of the Syndicate's oldest and most lucrative banking and investment houses&quot;) and Proctor House helps Premium Oil/Pentex manage their money and acquire their holdings. When Pentex became a holding company, Proctor merged a number of Syndicate fronts with the tech companies that Pentex was acquiring, creating the SPD. (OrigSyndConv, pg 36.)<br /> <br /> Premium Oil took the name Pentex before SPD was founded, and the SPD doesn't &quot;own&quot; Pentex. The SPD is a collaborative effort of Pentex's holdings and Proctor Houses's holdings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i> I attack people with giant insects both </i>on <i>and </i>off <i>the court.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","name":"Five Eyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"395"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T11:24:59-07:00","id":1083102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1077512-what-is-modus-operandi-of-nwo-against-vampires?p=1083091#post1083091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You typically find them in references to fast food joint O'Tolley's, Tellus Games, or the like. It tends to show up more in the artwork than the text, though it could be getting muddled in my head.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Interesting. I will find those mentions if I have opportunity. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1077512-what-is-modus-operandi-of-nwo-against-vampires?p=1083091#post1083091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">BoW? Is this distinct from Book of the Wyrm/BotW?</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Oops. Typo. Again. Yes, Hang it I fully intend to say Book of the Wyrm. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1077512-what-is-modus-operandi-of-nwo-against-vampires?p=1083091#post1083091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I knew about Premium Oil. It's listed as the primary cause or seed of what became Pentex in the rough timeline that the Werewolf Storyteller's Guide gave (the book that came with the Revised ST screen), since one of its early members had... a certain kind of help from beyond.</div> </div> </div> </div>I also remember that passage. Hmm...like I said, I really hate Technocracy-Pentex crossover. Sadly, it seems almost &quot;official&quot; the Syndicate founded and nurtured Pentex through Enlightened corporate merger and investment.<br /> <br /> And suddenly, they lost contact with the Pentex. And SPD functioned as its window to the Pentex. And they allowed it and did nothing about this development. Effectively, they ensured SPD's total autonomy.<br /> <br /> Oh where did that crossover go so much wrong? Where should I begin...?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4173,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","user":"Numinous","date":". 04-24-2017, 02:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","name":"Numinous","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T11:28:39-07:00","id":1083105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Five Eyes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1077512-what-is-modus-operandi-of-nwo-against-vampires?p=1083101#post1083101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Pentex's founder&quot; is a stretch.<br /> <br /> The Syndicate owned Proctor House (&quot;one of the Syndicate's oldest and most lucrative banking and investment houses&quot;) and Proctor House helps Premium Oil/Pentex manage their money and acquire their holdings. When Pentex became a holding company, Proctor merged a number of Syndicate fronts with the tech companies that Pentex was acquiring, creating the SPD. (OrigSyndConv, pg 36.)<br /> <br /> Premium Oil took the name Pentex before SPD was founded, and the SPD doesn't &quot;own&quot; Pentex. The SPD is a collaborative effort of Pentex's holdings and Proctor Houses's holdings.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have <i>never </i>said SPD does &quot;own&quot; Pentex or something remotely like it. I know it has been was started as basically joint North American Proctor House-Pentex project.<br /> <br /> But AFAIF, Syndicate <i>merged </i>Proctor House and Primium Oil somewhere in early 20th century and created Pentex. I think I have to re-check SyndConv to be certain. Unfortunately, it is currently unavailable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4173,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","user":"Numinous","date":". 04-24-2017, 02:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","name":"Numinous","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T11:35:37-07:00","id":1083110,"title":"","content":"Ah, found it.<br /> <br /> Syndicate Revised introduces the notion that Pentex is a merger of Proctor and Premium (pg54) - that's new in the Revised book, and it's either a mistake or a retcon. I'd honestly treat it as an error - it doesn't jibe with the previous material.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i> I attack people with giant insects both </i>on <i>and </i>off <i>the court.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","name":"Five Eyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"395"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T11:40:15-07:00","id":1083113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Five Eyes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1077512-what-is-modus-operandi-of-nwo-against-vampires?p=1083110#post1083110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, found it.<br /> <br /> Syndicate Revised introduces the notion that Pentex is a merger of Proctor and Premium (pg54) - that's new in the Revised book, and it's either a mistake or a retcon. I'd honestly treat it as an error - it doesn't jibe with the previous material.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm. I have always deemed it as retcon. I'm introduced in WoD after release of revised edition. I have learned revised first of all and then read original...and thought revised being the most 'canon' except its various crossover materials.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","name":"Numinous","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T11:51:58-07:00","id":1083121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1077512-what-is-modus-operandi-of-nwo-against-vampires?p=1083068#post1083068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a difference between a visible government with varying degrees of transparency throughout and an entirely opaque shadow government that nobody even knows exists.</div> </div> </div> </div>Technocracy is, technically(no pun intended), a &quot;legitimate&quot; opaque world government. Queen Victoria ratified the Technocratic Union and it served as shadowy counterpart of British and Continental Europe governments and implemented its internal, exterior and foreign policy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","name":"Numinous","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T13:05:08-07:00","id":1083146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Numinous</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Technocracy is, technically(no pun intended), a &quot;legitimate&quot; opaque world government. Queen Victoria ratified the Technocratic Union and it served as shadowy counterpart of British and Continental Europe governments and implemented its internal, exterior and foreign policy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh well, if Queen Victoria ratified it, then it's not shadowy at all!. I'm sure that I, being that I don't live in England, will totally not fell like a colony when I discover that my goverment it's a puppet of an imperialistic conspiracy from England. And I'm not going to blame them for all world problems real and imaginary. And then I'm not going to think that the whole vampiric thing it's a false flag attempt to conquer the world of this sci-fy conspiracy by creating a &quot;public enemy&quot; to distract the people while they take total control of the world.<br /> Meanwhile vampires are totally not trying to control the message to make themselves look better, or, at least, make the Technocracy look worse.<br /> <br /> <i>If everything goes right the Technocracy can raise the world against vampires, but if everything was right we would live in a scientific utopy where everyone it's an active and happy member of society that dreams of the wonders of science. We live in a world plagued by superstition, poverty, holly wars, and other problems that weren't aprooved by Control, so it seems not everything went right. Obviously the Technocracy isn't as omnipotent as they believe, and it's to be believed that vampires, if unable to keep the masquerade (that barely holds with every supernatural being contributing to it), at least they will try to manipulate the propaganda so their existense sounds less apocaliptical, or to make Technocracy seem evil (not hard, when people discover that they have been behind all crime in the world alongside leeches). At least they should be able to generate polemy, in this world it's stupidly easy to do</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T13:18:37-07:00","id":1083151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Numinous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1077512-what-is-modus-operandi-of-nwo-against-vampires?p=1083096#post1083096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No. Vampires have embedded ghouls in select areas - in other worlds, positions can exert most handy influence over local city and protect their masters and provide masters' needs and check masters' rivals.<br /> Oh, wait, in case of Giovanni, they embed ghouls to support their necromancy researches and fund it.<br /> <br /> In personal, Vampires are always acting shadowy on the surface level. Always.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not correct. Vampires also specifically embrace individuals in influential positions and have them act as their direct agents. They have to be more careful about it to avoid sunlight, but that's actually less hard than it appears. Influential people tend to have the, ahem, influence to make people work around their schedule, and a lot of influence-brokering goes on either after dark or remotely anyway. Power dinners, parties, after-hours parties, night classes, all-nighter working groups, detached functionary think tanks, conference calls, and if you're really in a pinch that's why Possession-suits exist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T04:35:43-07:00","id":1083405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Posthumanity</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1077512-what-is-modus-operandi-of-nwo-against-vampires?p=1077581#post1077581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So Masquerade is being maintained even Sabbat-held city such as Montreal or Mexico City?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's called &quot;the silence of the blood&quot; and it's to keep the legions of hunters at bay (the various hunter factions are generally way more concerned about killing Sabbat than they are with killing Camarilla or Anarchs).<br /> <br /> Plus it prevents the Camarilla from finding them and wiping them out too. The cam is more powerful and its members more numerous than the Sabbat according to the source material, that's why the Cam is won top and the Sabbat isn't","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3148-zennis","name":"Zennis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T18:01:45-07:00","id":1083765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zennis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1077512-what-is-modus-operandi-of-nwo-against-vampires?p=1083405#post1083405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's called &quot;the silence of the blood&quot; and it's to keep the legions of hunters at bay (the various hunter factions are generally way more concerned about killing Sabbat than they are with killing Camarilla or Anarchs).<br /> <br /> Plus it prevents the Camarilla from finding them and wiping them out too. The cam is more powerful and its members more numerous than the Sabbat according to the source material, that's why the Cam is won top and the Sabbat isn't</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, while the Sabbat may despise the Masquerade, they nonetheless maintain it themselves, in their own way. It's just common sense. Between hunters, the Camarilla, and their own more prudent sect-mates, individual Sabbat licks disregarding the Masquerade tends to be a self-correcting problem. Those who can't get with the program die off, strengthening the sect as a whole. It's very Darwinian in that regard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}